 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "And May is all sweet the morning,\nIs all sweet the night after,\nHeaven and earth have turned to flower,\nWhat else do they call beauty?\nO Night, whose pale hand seals up life's fire,\nAll things are smooth and gay as grasses grow,\nAs wind that gives no sound of its power\nThe dark night around it blows from afar,\nHow fast their lightnings run away\nA woman's face is lovely,\nA man's face in fire made clear; alas,\nIf night were not so lovely,",
